The writer of this email could sound Encouraging, Appreciative, Informal, and Confident to the reader. 

The writer uses an Informal tone in addressing the recipient with "Hi Jen" and offers somewhat casual benefits - "There's a coffee in it for you!". They are Appreciative, asking for assistance and valuing feedback with statements like "I'd appreciate your input." This email also indicates an Encouraging tone, inviting feedback and implying a collegial, cooperative atmosphere - "Can we catch up today?". There's an element of Confidence too, as the writer is not shy about asking for help and discussing a work-related matter (the presentation). 

The email is properly punctuated, the word choice is friendly, and the phrasing straightforward, which all add to these tones. The sentences are properly capitalized, contributing further to the overall appropriate tone of the email.

